This repository is covered by two licences, because it holds two different
kinds of work.

  SOURCE CODE      MIT — the full text below.
                   Everything under app/, lib/, components/, mcp/, scripts/,
                   messages/ and the build configuration.

  CONTENT          CC BY 4.0 — see LICENSE-CONTENT.
                   Everything under content/ and skills/, and every artifact
                   generated from it: the rendered pages, the JSON APIs,
                   llms.txt, llms-full.txt, the knowledge graph and the
                   payloads returned by the MCP endpoint.

Two licences rather than one because CC BY is not a software licence and MIT is
not a content licence. Applying either to both would leave the terms ambiguous
exactly where someone evaluating reuse looks first.

